# =============================================================================
#  accepted.conf  ·  copy to <your-repo>/_deploy/accepted.conf and fill it in
# =============================================================================
#  Read by the master gate. This is NOT shell: it is parsed, never executed.
#
#  WHAT IT IS
#  ----------
#  An accepted failure is a BUSINESS DECISION ALREADY TAKEN, not an unfixed
#  defect. It does not count towards the verdict, but it is still measured and
#  it still appears in the receipt with its name, its reason, who signed it and
#  until when.
#
#  WHY IT EXISTS
#  -------------
#  The gate could not tell OUR defect from the CLIENT's decision: it treated
#  "the favicon weighs 320 KB" exactly like "the client has not decided how long
#  leads are retained". Measured on a real site: of its 8 FAILs, ZERO were
#  defects of the tree. Without this, no site can be green while a decision is
#  pending — and there are always decisions pending.
#  **A gate that can never be satisfied is a gate somebody switches off.**
#
#  WHAT IT IS **NOT**
#  ------------------
#  · NOT the "anyway" flag. That is for things NOT LOOKED AT (NOT VERIFIED) and
#    it does not touch a red. A red is still a hard stop.
#  · NOT for covering up OUR defect. If it is fixed by writing code, write code.
#  · NOT for covering up a FALSE POSITIVE. That hides it on this site and leaves
#    it alive on every other one. Fix it in the gate.
#
#  THE FIVE LOCKS
#  --------------
#  1 · It lives in the REPO, in version control. A command-line flag gets copied
#      and pasted without thinking; a file gets reviewed in a diff.
#  2 · FIVE MANDATORY FIELDS. If one is missing the entry is void, it is said
#      out loud, and the failure keeps counting.
#  3 · You accept a FINDING, not a CHECK. It matches against the `FINGERPRINT`
#      line the report prints under each FAIL. If the finding changes, IT COUNTS
#      AGAIN.
#  4 · IT EXPIRES: 90 days by default, hard ceiling 180 (an `UNTIL` beyond the
#      ceiling is rejected outright, not trimmed), warning at 14 days out.
#  5 · Some things can never be accepted; that list lives in the gate, not here.
#      Today: cookies before consent, a pre-ticked box, no cookie/privacy page
#      at all, a legal policy live in draft, and an internal path exposed.
#      The criterion: the harm falls on the VISITOR and is invisible to us.
#
#  HOW TO FILL IT IN
#  -----------------
#    perl gates/qa-master.pl <URL> --repo DIR --candidate
#  and copy, VERBATIM, the `FINGERPRINT` line printed under the FAIL.
#  When a check emits no evidence (it is binary and site-wide) the fingerprint
#  it prints is `WHOLE-CHECK`, and that is what goes here. It is not a wildcard:
#  if the finding DOES carry evidence, `WHOLE-CHECK` matches nothing.
#
#  THE THREE FINGERPRINT SHAPES, AND WHAT EACH MEANS
#  -------------------------------------------------
#    DATA=... WHERE=...      the WHERE is the ENTIRE evidence for the finding.
#    DATA=... EV=<8 hex>     the finding has MORE evidence than fits on screen
#                            (25 pages, 40 resources...). The report prints three
#                            or four; the EV summarises the WHOLE SET. If a
#                            single one enters or leaves, the EV changes and the
#                            acceptance stops matching. To read the full list
#                            BEFORE signing:  --evidence
#    DATA=... EVS=<8 hex>    the same, but the check measured a SAMPLE, not the
#                            whole site (performance looks at 3 pages of 25).
#                            Accepting this is NOT accepting that the rest is
#                            clean: it is accepting what was looked at. The
#                            receipt says so in those words, and whoever
#                            deploys sees it.
#
#  WHY A HASH AND NOT THE LIST. Because this line gets read in a diff: with 25
#  paths inside it would be 3 KB and the file would stop being reviewable, which
#  is the FIRST lock of the whole mechanism. The `DATA` beside it shows at a
#  glance WHAT is accepted; the hash ties the acceptance to the exact set.
#
#  THE HOLE THIS CLOSED, so it does not reopen: the fingerprint used to be
#  computed over what was PRINTED. On one site an accessibility check reported
#  "25 of 25 pages" and listed 4; making one of the other 21 worse did NOT move
#  the fingerprint, and the failure stayed silenced. It failed towards the
#  unsafe side.
# =============================================================================

[ACCEPTED]
# The check id, exactly as the report prints it.
CHECK:     MED-09
# The exact FINGERPRINT. Copied from the report, never written from memory.
FINDING:   WHOLE-CHECK
# Why this is not a defect of ours. If nobody knows why it is pending, write
# that it is pending AND WHO DECIDES. An invented reason is worse than none: it
# looks like a decision and it is not.
REASON:    PENDING DECISION: how many months leads are retained is the client's legal call.
# Who signs. A person, with a name. Not "the team".
ACCEPTS:   Firstname Lastname
# When it was accepted (YYYY-MM-DD).
DATE:      2026-08-11
# Optional. Defaults to DATE + 90 days; hard ceiling is 180.
UNTIL:     2026-09-10
